                "quoted_status_profile_username": "politico",
                "reply_count": 9,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "For 40 days, President Trump and Republicans refused to negotiate a bipartisan budget deal that prevents healthcare costs from skyrocketing. In CA50, 28,000 people will face higher costs if we don't extend ACA tax credits. We cannot afford to wait, yet this deal does nothing to address this crisis.\u00a0\n\nWe also have no assurance that the President won\u2019t continue to disrespect and ignore appropriations law. He already did it, with no pushback from Speaker Johnson. How can we trust him to spend the funds as directed by Congress now?\n\nWhen Speaker Johnson finally brings the House back into session on this, I'm voting no.",
                "text_lang": "en",
